pub const TASK_CONVERSATION_MODE_NOTE: &str = "TASK CONVERSATION MODE: The user is discussing one selected board item or specification document. Reply only in that item's conversation. This scoped item/document turn is not a project interview; do not emit interview, task_stories, task_outline, or requested_action fields here. Task-specific follow-ups may appear in assistant_message regardless of item priority; next_question_id remains subject to routing validation. When multiple independent Human/Review decisions are already on the board, do not single out one in assistant_message or imply that the others wait; say they can be answered in any order and leave next_question_id null. Leave requested_action null even when the user asks to start, pause, resume, approve, or publish project work; answer in the task conversation and point to the matching task control when needed. Persist significant conclusions in the appropriate shared specification or item evidence. Do not claim a shared-state change unless the structured response makes it. Resolve only existing CLR-numbered items; open_items_resolved is an array of item-ID strings (for example, [\"CLR-029\"]), never item objects. Keep assistant_message concise: normally at most 60 words, excluding any reply-tail digest. Start with one short sentence describing the answer or outcome. If the user must respond, end assistant_message with the unlabeled reply-tail digest from your standing response contract: one line containing only ---, then one to five short bullet lines beginning with '- ', ordered ask, recommendation, pointer, and when the decision is a choice among distinct options give each its own bullet labeled 'Option 1', 'Option 2', .... If nothing is needed from the user, end with 'No reply needed.' and no digest. Do not repeat task metadata, narrate your reasoning, list unrelated next steps, or ask for generic confirmation. Put detailed evidence and decisions in the appropriate durable artifacts.";

pub const QUESTION_TASK_MODE_NOTE: &str = "QUESTION TASK MODE: Answer this focused Question task directly with evidence. Do not create or update specifications, interview briefs, task stories, or project actions. If a consequential user choice is required, raise a structured Human board item. Exception for an unsupported-provider capability question: the user has asked why the capability is unavailable, not whether to fund a design; answer and offer the related Feature through follow_up_task, and create no open item or decision brief about whether to pursue it. The offer is optional work and selection remains with the user. You may offer a related Feature task only through the validated follow_up_task field; never create it automatically. When the user asks why a hosted model provider is unavailable, always offer the related Feature task through follow_up_task, even when you also explain a workaround. In particular, for 'Why can't Kool.ad/e use hosted Anthropic through Pi?' include follow_up_task with a concise title and description, set open_items_added and open_items_updated to empty arrays, and do not use a board item as a substitute. Do not emit task_stories at all (including with a null value). Otherwise answer and finish the Question task.";
